From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 22:21:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/apple: power a T8132 external DCP down with
 nothing attached

With nothing attached, dispext0_cpu and dispext1_cpu stay on and the
dcpext firmware DARTs stay active for as long as the machine runs:
nothing ever powers an idle dcpext down.

Power it down once nothing has been attached for dcpext_idle_ms
(appledrm.dcpext_idle_ms, 5 s; 0 turns it off). The decision
(dcp-m4-ext-idle.h) runs under hpd_mutex with the driver's inputs:
DPTX ports, the Type-C route, the HDMI hot-plug level, the HDMI
start, a queued Type-C reconnect and unanswered teardown calls; the
session adds its own. It is looked at again whenever what is attached
changes (a display released, a route ended, an HDMI hot-plug edge, a
sink gone) and, while something only passes, after the delay.

Hot-plug keeps working: a display only appears through the AP, and
every way it does asks the firmware to connect first. A DPTX connect,
and any AFK command, powers the DCP up before it talks to it
(dcp_t8132_idle_wake()); a message that would still reach it
stopped is not sent and is logged. System sleep, remove and shutdown
stop the policy first; shutdown powers the DCP up for its unbind.
Resume powers it up as before, and the policy takes it down again.

The host selftests that build afk.c, dcp.c or dcp-fabric.c functions
stub the two hooks, as they stub the other T8132 ones.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5
(cherry picked from commit 99e7cbf5ef8e2fbc49f7cc5ee87e1a33502f14bb)
